bkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"78b11a2973fed59c04a40535078f11efd5d02d4f4c026a7d6fc021e9c4421917","event_uuid":"f3778a9e-8f66-4fd5-833d-28c952da42d1","position":{"commit_sha":"e637a70ae6f31280a75321d0df4a880097865b06","position":"1786524397323373001-f3778a9e-8f66-4fd5-833d-28c952da42d1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"60fdbcc4370a0a02438ec398158ce7ebcaf9bce03665066ec1cd099cd48c06ef","event_uuid":"724a33f2-1062-47a9-8d6b-b92f39f067fc","position":{"commit_sha":"8cffcd0b67c160edb1b2966f3bb82ead48fd8686","position":"1786524408556590001-724a33f2-1062-47a9-8d6b-b92f39f067fc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ee924b0b65b325a146c9a5e0ee7e6a1d5474cc0fe1b38913a90590a357459cc0","event_uuid":"96a9736d-6eda-4c10-b1e7-fb881201b2c1","position":{"commit_sha":"8cffcd0b67c160edb1b2966f3bb82ead48fd8686","position":"1786524409245378001-96a9736d-6eda-4c10-b1e7-fb881201b2c1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a6f386a7566f50d4ac4c21c67ea1bd72a37d7163e46deb5e1cef0d9bb3e14b13","event_uuid":"94e92c64-009d-43b0-8e98-11672fe97327","position":{"commit_sha":"948bb3b6f65cee3bc9b01a55d71bff5f238515fd","position":"1786524916625614498-94e92c64-009d-43b0-8e98-11672fe97327"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[],"created_at":1786517403248052001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"534b2440-04ce-48ab-a562-9bafe0660016","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"9a71-ba9b-89d0-4cb8"},{"link_uuid":"94e92c64-009d-43b0-8e98-11672fe97327","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ce44-bcbb-f486-444b"}],"description":"# Reconcile Bridge fails a converged pass when re-dispatch hits a disabled workflow\n\n## Impact, stated first\n\nTwo Reconcile Bridge runs (31129551929, 31129431096) **converged the reconcile\nsuccessfully** and were still marked RED, because the final opt-in re-dispatch step\ncould not queue the next run. A red run here trips the heartbeat/alerting path for a\nnon-problem, and it makes a genuine bridge outage harder to see among false reds.\n\n## Confirmed root cause (evidence)\n\nRun 31129551929's log tail carries exactly one `::error` — from the re-dispatch step:\n\n```\ncould not create workflow dispatch event: HTTP 422: Cannot trigger a\n'workflow_dispatch' on a disabled workflow\n(https://api.github.com/repos/navapbc/rebar/actions/workflows/302389202/dispatches)\n```\n\nThe step `Re-dispatch to sustain the continuous loop (opt-in)` in\n`.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml` runs under `set -euo pipefail` and ends with a\nbare `gh workflow run ...`. When the workflow is disabled, `gh` exits non-zero, so\n`pipefail` fails the step and therefore the whole job — **after** the reconcile step has\nalready converged and delivered.\n\nWorkflow 302389202 is `active` again today, so the disabled state was transient. The\ndefect is not the disabled state; it is that a transient inability to re-seed the loop is\ntreated as a pass failure.\n\n## Why this is safe to downgrade\n\nThe workflow header already documents the `*/20` schedule as the backstop for exactly\nthis case: \"The `*/20` schedule stays as a backstop that re-seeds the chain if it ever\nstops.\" So a failed re-dispatch is already a designed-for, self-healing condition — the\nchain restarts from the schedule. Failing the job adds no recovery, only noise.\n\nThe downgrade is deliberately narrow: **only** an HTTP 422 naming a disabled workflow\nbecomes benign. Every other re-dispatch failure (auth, 404, network, rate limit) stays\nfatal, so a genuinely broken re-dispatch is still loud.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. In `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml`, stop letting the bare `gh workflow run`\n   exit status fail the step. Capture its combined output and exit status explicitly\n   (without disabling `pipefail` for the rest of the step).\n2. On success: keep the existing informational log line, exit 0.\n3. On failure whose output matches the disabled-workflow 422 signature (an HTTP 422\n   together with the `disabled workflow` phrase): emit a GitHub `::warning` that names\n   the condition and points at the `*/20` schedule backstop, then exit 0.\n4. On any other failure: re-emit the captured output and exit non-zero, preserving\n   today's fail-loud behavior.\n5. Update the step's comment block to record why the 422-disabled case is benign\n   (backstop schedule) and that all other failures remain fatal.\n\n## Scope / non-goals\n\n- No change to the reconcile or delivery steps.\n- No change to `RECONCILE_CONTINUOUS` opt-in semantics or the `*/20` schedule.\n- No new secrets, credentials, permissions, or infrastructure. The step keeps the\n  `actions: write` permission it already has.\n- Does not touch the two sibling bridge-delivery bugs (`freeborn-dizzy-raven`,\n  `subzero-locustal-junebug`), which are distinct defects in the git delivery path.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: A test asserts that the re-dispatch step in\n  `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml` does not end in a bare unguarded\n  `gh workflow run` invocation — i.e. its exit status is captured and branched on rather\n  than being allowed to fail the step directly.\n- [ ] AC2: A test asserts the step's failure branch matches the disabled-workflow 422\n  signature (both the `422` token and the `disabled workflow` phrase must be required, so\n  an unrelated 422 does not go benign).\n- [ ] AC3: A test asserts the benign branch emits a `::warning` (not `::error`) and that\n  the non-matching branch still exits non-zero.\n- [ ] AC4: `actionlint`/workflow-lint gates covering `reconcile-bridge.yml` pass on the\n  edited file (the repo's existing workflow-lint test suite is green).\n- [ ] AC5: `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass, and the full existing bridge/workflow\n  test selection passes unchanged.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml","reason":"Guard the opt-in re-dispatch step so a disabled-workflow HTTP 422 is a benign warn+exit 0 while every other failure stays fatal"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py","reason":"Assert the re-dispatch step captures gh exit status, requires both the 422 and disabled-workflow tokens, and warns rather than errors on the benign branch"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","ce44-bcbb-f486-444b"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"724a33f2-1062-47a9-8d6b-b92f39f067fc","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"8aed-e264-7112-4c2f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Reconcile Bridge continuous-loop re-dispatch fails HTTP 422 on a disabled workflow","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b50dae84-87a1-421a-a057-5bdffee5318b","534b2440-04ce-48ab-a562-9bafe0660016","4adf68d8-5d7d-4a94-b1ef-536f30390927","f3778a9e-8f66-4fd5-833d-28c952da42d1","724a33f2-1062-47a9-8d6b-b92f39f067fc","96a9736d-6eda-4c10-b1e7-fb881201b2c1","94e92c64-009d-43b0-8e98-11672fe97327"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786524916625614499,"uuid":"0fb7e09a-0df9-4f93-836b-ff855d283bb9"}